      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "${(-3)}^{3}+{4}^{3}=$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. \n\nFirst, we compute the exponents:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-3)}^{3}+{4}^{3}=(-27)+64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-27)+64 & = \\\\ -27+64 & = \\\\ 37\\end{aligned}\n$$",
