      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "${6}^{3}÷{(-3)}^{2}+10=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate the given expression, we use PEMDAS. \n\nFirst, we compute the exponent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{6}^{3}÷{(-3)}^{2}+10 & =216÷9+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we divide:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}216÷9+10 & =24+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we add:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}24+10 & =34\\end{aligned}\n$$",
