      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the value of ${(-3+1.9)}^{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, we perform the operation inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-3+1.9)}^{2} & ={(-1.1)}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the exponent:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(-1.1)}^{2} & =1.21\\end{aligned}\n$$",
