      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$(-18)÷((-3)^{4}÷9)=${{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, consider the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{4}÷9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-3)^{4}÷9 & = \\\\ 81÷9 & = \\\\ \\frac{81}{9} & = \\\\ 9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-18)÷((-3)^{4}÷9) & = \\\\ (-18)÷9 & = \\\\ \\frac{(-18)}{9} & = \\\\ -\\frac{18}{9} & = \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
