    "q-100159": {
      "dom_id": "step-q100159",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Evaluate $(3\\times (-5)^{2})÷\\frac{5}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "To evaluate this expression, we use PEMDAS.\n\nFirst, consider the expression inside the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\times (-5)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying PEMDAS to this expression, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3\\times (-5)^{2} & = \\\\ 3\\times 25 & = \\\\ 75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3\\times (-5)^{2})÷\\frac{5}{2} & = \\\\ 75÷\\frac{5}{2} & = \\\\ 75\\times \\frac{2}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{75}{1}\\times \\frac{2}{5} & = \\\\ \\frac{75\\times 2}{1\\times 5} & = \\\\ \\frac{150}{5} & = \\\\ 30\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
